# The `f1aV0p` reduction of set (e)

The label-split certificate of `QED.Algebra.IBPCertSector` reduces the projected combination `Y - (d
- 1)² T₁` of the lower-loop piece `f1a_V0` (topology `f1a`, 0 mass-counterterm insertions)
(`QED.ThreeLoopE.SetECert.f1aV0pTarget`, integrals in scaleless sectors dropped) to the Kira masters
`QED.ThreeLoopE.SetECert.f1aV0pMasters` of the family `QED.ThreeLoopE.SetECert.f1a`.

## Main statements

* `QED.ThreeLoopE.SetECert.f1aV0p_reduction_of_den`: at every `d` with `q(d) ≠ 0`, for every family
  of values satisfying the hypotheses at `d`, the target combination equals the certified
  combination of the masters.
* `QED.ThreeLoopE.SetECert.f1aV0p_reduction`: the same off a finite set of `d`.

Generated by `gen.py` (offline cache `setecert/fams`); do not edit. Integers are written as `.ofNat
n` and `.negSucc n` (`= -n - 1`).
-/

